<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.1: </span>Three pairwise non-isotopic resolvable <math id="A1.F1.m320" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(7\times 15,35)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>35</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(7\times 15,35)</annotation></semantics></math>-triple arrays corresponding to the Kirkman parade ‘1b’, one of two resolutions of <math id="A1.F1.m321" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\PG(3,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>PG</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\PG(3,2)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The top array is isotopic to the triple array in Figure <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5.1 Resolvable triple arrays ‣ 5 Triple arrays via resolutions ‣ Resolvable Triple Arrays" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, originally found by McSorley, Phillips, Wallis and Yucas <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">mcsorleyDoubleArraysTriple2005a</span>]</cite>.
The top and middle triple arrays share the same underlying unordered triple array, labeled as <math id="A1.F1.m322" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{6}</annotation></semantics></math> in Table <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table A.1 ‣ Appendix A Counts of resolvable (7×15,35)-triple arrays ‣ Resolvable Triple Arrays" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, while the bottom triple array is the unique (up to isotopism) ordering of <math id="A1.F1.m323" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{7}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
